{"type":"text","timestamp":1794311997367,"sessionID":"ses_e3abb1ca8ffeerep4FBuX0hWYx","part":{"id":"prt_1c553cfbb001i3sJwWjZzCTeRG","sessionID":"ses_e3abb1ca8ffeerep4FBuX0hWYx","messageID":"msg_1c553bbb900104r4InyvmKOD2s","type":"text","text":"All 6 tests pass. Here's a summary of the changes:\n\n**`calc/lexer.py`** — Extended to support:\n- Decimal numbers (`1.5`) via `float` conversion\n- New operators: `*`, `/`, `%`, `**` (with `**` token merging)\n- Parentheses `(`, `)` as `LPAREN`/`RPAREN` tokens\n- Identifiers as `NAME` (variables) or `FUNC` (built-in functions)\n- Comma `,` as `COMMA` token for function arguments\n- Empty input raises `CalcError`\n\n**`calc/parser.py`** — Rewritten as a recursive-descent parser with proper precedence:\n1. `parse_add` — `+`, `-` (left associative, lowest)\n2. `parse_mul` — `*`, `/`, `%` (left associative)\n3. `parse_unary` — unary `-`\n4. `parse_power` — `**` (right associative, tighter than unary minus)\n5. `parse_primary` — numbers, variables, function calls, parenthesized expressions\n- Trailing tokens after parsing raise `CalcError`\n\n**`calc/evaluator.py`** — Extended to handle:\n- Binary operations including `*`, `/`, `%`, `**` with division/modulo-by-zero checks\n- Unary minus\n- Variable lookup from `env` with `CalcError` for unknown variables\n- Built-in functions `min`, `max`, `abs` with argument count validation","time":{"start":1794311966651,"end":1794311997367}}}
